WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.858 --> 00:00:04.492
In the plant stands the frame of the filling unit for line 3.

2
00:00:05.168 --> 00:00:07.815
It has to carry the filled tank, for years.

3
00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:11.256
A load is a force the frame has to carry.

4
00:00:11.915 --> 00:00:16.536
Strength is how much load the steel takes before it bends for good or breaks.

5
00:00:17.537 --> 00:00:19.151
Four topics follow the frame.

6
00:00:19.877 --> 00:00:23.906
The first two are about what the frame carries and what the steel takes.

7
00:00:24.925 --> 00:00:29.488
The last two are about how the frame can still break and which steel you choose.

8
00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:34.027
The first topic is Forces, moments and stress.

9
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.348
The frame carries the weight of the filled tank.

10
00:00:38.074 --> 00:00:40.048
Every filling also gives a shock.

11
00:00:41.097 --> 00:00:42.688
Stress is force per area.

12
00:00:43.385 --> 00:00:47.390
The same force is harmless to a thick bar and fatal to a thin one.

13
00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:51.049
The frame will soon go to hall B by crane.

14
00:00:51.758 --> 00:00:55.206
For that we read the working load limit on the tag of the sling.

15
00:00:56.507 --> 00:00:59.688
The second topic is Material strength and testing.

16
00:01:00.418 --> 00:01:03.309
A bar from the steel of the frame goes to the lab.

17
00:01:04.358 --> 00:01:07.040
A machine pulls the bar until it breaks.

18
00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.445
At the yield strength it starts to bend for good.

19
00:01:11.213 --> 00:01:12.722
The frame stays below it.

20
00:01:13.846 --> 00:01:16.400
For strength we often use a tensile test.

21
00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:20.007
The third topic is Fatigue and failure.

22
00:01:20.732 --> 00:01:24.296
The frame is strong enough and can still break after months.

23
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.609
A load that comes back millions of times grows a crack,

24
00:01:28.923 --> 00:01:30.711
even below the yield strength.

25
00:01:31.562 --> 00:01:33.338
It starts at a sharp corner.

26
00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:37.447
We often read a broken part with fractography.

27
00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:42.181
The fourth topic is Heat treatment and material choice.

28
00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.998
The frame is made of structural steel from the rack, because it is strong,

29
00:01:47.092 --> 00:01:48.613
stiff and easy to weld.

30
00:01:49.714 --> 00:01:52.547
A heat treatment heats steel and quenches it.

31
00:01:53.303 --> 00:01:54.766
Then it is hard but brittle.

32
00:01:55.535 --> 00:01:57.323
Tempering makes it tougher again.

33
00:01:58.003 --> 00:02:00.522
Steel that is too hard is difficult to mill.

34
00:02:01.499 --> 00:02:04.576
For heat treatment we often use a hardness test.

35
00:02:05.623 --> 00:02:07.806
The steel is chosen and tested.

36
00:02:08.546 --> 00:02:10.485
A block of it goes to the workshop.

37
00:02:11.228 --> 00:02:13.724
The plate of the unit is made from it there.

38
00:02:15.058 --> 00:02:16.231
This is the whole map.

39
00:02:16.976 --> 00:02:20.970
Materials and strength is the first station of Making things.

40
00:02:21.994 --> 00:02:23.689
Every topic has four levels.

41
00:02:24.668 --> 00:02:27.792
Start with Force, weight and torque, at Basics level.

42
00:02:28.497 --> 00:02:30.866
That lesson shows what the frame carries.

43
00:02:31.903 --> 00:02:35.061
At Working knowledge level it is about stress and strain,

44
00:02:35.247 --> 00:02:38.579
test results, a broken part and heat treatment.

45
00:02:39.664 --> 00:02:41.998
At Advanced level it is about toughness,

46
00:02:42.171 --> 00:02:46.165
fatigue life, steel names and bending in beams and shafts.

47
00:02:47.178 --> 00:02:50.092
At Expert level it is about an FEA plot,

48
00:02:50.173 --> 00:02:54.550
material certificates, welded fatigue and substituting materials.

49
00:02:55.558 --> 00:02:59.215
Every lesson and film in this module has a place on this map.
